# Use in-repo skills

Before implementing, debugging, deploying, or writing substantial prose, **load and follow** the matching skill under [`.ox-agent/skills/`](../../.ox-agent/skills/) — also reachable via the [`.agents/skills/`](../../.agents/skills/) and [`.claude/skills/`](../../.claude/skills/) symlinks. Do not invent a parallel workflow when a project skill already covers the task.

## How to pick a skill

1. Scan skill names/descriptions in `.ox-agent/skills/*/SKILL.md`.
2. Read the skill file immediately when it matches the task.
3. Prefer project skills over generic habits or external defaults.
4. Spec/planning work runs through **ox-agent work items**, not loose docs: `ox-agent start <title>` opens the item, then the `normal` pipeline stages (discovery → brainstorming → specification → planning → implementation) map onto the ox-owned skills below. Human questions go through durable `ox-agent input` requests — never synchronous prompts.

## Common mappings

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|--------|
| `apps/web` UI / `.tsrx` / Octane | [octane](../../.ox-agent/skills/octane/SKILL.md) |
| New or reshaped visual UI | [frontend-design](../../.ox-agent/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md), [web-design-guidelines](../../.ox-agent/skills/web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md) when auditing |
| Rust API / async / idioms | [rust-async-patterns](../../.ox-agent/skills/rust-async-patterns/SKILL.md), [rust-best-practices](../../.ox-agent/skills/rust-best-practices/SKILL.md) |
| Test-first / red-green | [tdd](../../.ox-agent/skills/tdd/SKILL.md) |
| Hard bugs / regressions | [diagnosing-bugs](../../.ox-agent/skills/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md) |
| Module design / seams | [codebase-design](../../.ox-agent/skills/codebase-design/SKILL.md), [improve-codebase-architecture](../../.ox-agent/skills/improve-codebase-architecture/SKILL.md) |
| Railway / cloud deploy / flags | [use-railway](../../.ox-agent/skills/use-railway/SKILL.md) |
| User-facing prose finalize | [clean-user-facing-text](../../.ox-agent/skills/clean-user-facing-text/SKILL.md) (also [`.cursor/rules/clean-user-facing-text.mdc`](clean-user-facing-text.mdc)) |
| AI watermark / provenance strip | [remove-ai-marks](../../.ox-agent/skills/remove-ai-marks/SKILL.md) |
| Spec / planning for significant work | `ox-agent start` + [discover-context](../../.ox-agent/skills/discover-context/SKILL.md), [specify](../../.ox-agent/skills/specify/SKILL.md), [multi-stage-plan](../../.ox-agent/skills/multi-stage-plan/SKILL.md) |
| Decision records | [adr](../../.ox-agent/skills/adr/SKILL.md) → `context/decisions/` |
| Security review | [security-review](../../.ox-agent/skills/security-review/SKILL.md), [code-review](../../.ox-agent/skills/code-review/SKILL.md) |

Durable knowledge lives under `.ox-agent/context/` — product docs, standards, ADRs, and the spec record (including the read-only `_archive/` provenance). `ox-agent context index` rebuilds the catalog after edits.

## Do not

- Skip a matching skill because the change “looks small.”
- Re-derive Octane, Railway, or watermark procedures from memory when the skill exists.
- Edit ox-owned materialized files (`.ox-agent/skills`, `schemas`, `workflows`, `pipelines`, `lifecycle`, `integrations`) in place — add extension skills as new directories instead.
